# Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so anything excluded there is still sent as build context
# unless it is repeated here. Two concrete problems this file solves, both measured:
#
#  1. A build FAILS outright on unreadable transient directories. `docker build -f
#     scripts/dogfood/Dockerfile.source .` died with
#     `error from sender: open .pytest_tmp_review_<hex>: Access is denied` -- a gitignored pytest
#     temp directory left by a concurrent test run. The context sender walks the whole tree and
#     has no idea the directory is disposable.
#  2. Without these entries the context includes `target/` (Rust build artifacts, easily
#     gigabytes), `.venv/`, and the full `.git/` history, which is uploaded to the daemon on every
#     build.
#
# Keep this in sync with .gitignore for the transient/build-output entries. It deliberately does
# NOT exclude src/, rust_core/, tests/, or scripts/ -- Dockerfile.source builds the working tree
# and needs all of them.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Python transients.
#
# NOTE THE `**/` PREFIXES. Docker ignore patterns are anchored at the context ROOT unless they
# start with `**/`, so a bare `.venv/` excludes only the top-level one. A nested `rust_core/.venv/`
# survived that and broke the build with `invalid file request rust_core/.venv/bin/python` -- a
# venv symlink pointing outside the context. Anchor-by-default is the trap here; every transient
# pattern below is therefore `**/`-prefixed.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_tmp_*/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.hypothesis/
**/*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Transient scratch/repro directories left by test and agent sessions. These are the ones that
# actually BREAK the build rather than merely bloat it: the context sender cannot open some of
# them ("Access is denied") and aborts the whole build. Measured offenders at the repo root
# included `.pytest_tmp_review_<hex>/` and `.tmp_council_20260803_f2/`; the glob covers the family
# rather than naming instances, because naming instances is how this recurs.
**/.tmp/
**/.tmp*/

# Rust build output (the single largest context contributor)
**/target/

# Node
**/node_modules/

# Local tool + agent state
.orchestrator/
.tensor-grep/
_tg_refs/
.claude/settings.local.json
.factory/
.gemini/

# Benchmark corpora and generated data (large, never needed to build the binary)
bench_data/
bench_ast_data/
gpu_bench_data/
benchmarks/bench_data/
benchmarks/bench_ast_data/
benchmarks/gpu_bench_data/
benchmarks/external_repos/

# Editor/OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
